NAME
       setjmp, longjmp - non-local jump

SYNOPSIS
       #include <setjmp.h>

       int  setjmp(jmp_buf env);
       void longjmp(jmp_buf env, int val);

DESCRIPTION
       setjmp saves the machine state and returns 0. A later longjmp
       makes it appear to return again, this time with VAL, or 1 when
       VAL is 0.

       The function that called setjmp must not have returned yet.
       Local variables that are not volatile may hold stale values
       after the jump.

SEE ALSO
       signal(3), abort(3)
